  "description": "Bimba M3′ bridge artifact — the 3:3/4:2 crossing represented as an ordered, source-backed scene traversal. Coordinates: #3-5 The 360° Mythic Synthesis Wheel; #3-5-5/0 Axis Mundi — Central Unity Origin; #3-5-5/0-0/360 Alpha-Omega Point; cardinal anchors #3-5-1 North, #3-5-3 East, #3-5-2 South, #3-5-4 West. M′ instrument: M3′ Journey/Scenes ↔ real Expression Scenes (L5-TECHNE-DUAL-READING-LOCK §9; the lock's first canonical traversal §12 ends in Return). Every scene frame names the exact coordinate it stands on (scene character + formation labels); Journey persists through real Scene refs, no second scene ontology. Inherited profile: bimba-corpus-base → family-mahamaya-transcription (wheel_grammar). Variation (source-backed): the order Alpha-Omega → N → E → S → W → Axis Mundi follows the anchors the registry itself declares; compass positions present each anchor's own compass name; the 360 leaves are represented by #3-5-5/0-0/360, not staged leaf-by-leaf (engine journey cap 64 scenes — honest limitation). Relations cited: bimba:relation:3560ab427ec0539c02abbf5e (#3-5 → #3-5-5/0) and bimba:relation:851f7f0ee11a86f2fe3ebc02 (#3-5 → #3-5-1), both HAS_INTERNAL_COMPONENT. Sources: registry_revision 259a2f496c5f3a76d31e5c480dc9afdb45ad1282a7034cc28c528c39a71442e4 at QL-MEF e87d6bcef81d005e848b978a11a0ab53b7739973. Binding record: bindings/bimba-m3-axis-mundi-wheel.binding.json.",
